{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1482191-creating-ame-no-ohabari-as-a-relic","id":1482191,"title":"Creating Ame-no-ohabari as a relic.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-28T13:36:14-07:00","id":1482191,"title":"Creating Ame-no-ohabari as a relic.","content":"So, When Izanagi killed his last born, Kagu-tsuchi, he did so with a Totsuka-no-Tsurugi, a &quot;Sword of Ten Hand Breadths&quot; later called Ame-no-Ohabari, As the dead god fell, the volcanos of Japan were formed and where blood spattered off the blade, a number of gods including Takemakizuchi were born. <br /> <br /> I was thinking about giving the sword to a player as a Relic, but couldn't for the life of me decide what it could do. It has off hand associations with Sky, Water and Fire due to killing a fire deity and creating Kami of both the air and water. Its capable of dismembering a greater kami in the right hands... and then it disappears from mythology... so what do I make it capable of?<br /> <br /> I was thinking giving it the brutal tag and also granting it a +2e when facing Kami but I worry that that is both too powerful and two specific. I just don't know. any out of the box ideas from you guys?<br /> <br /> With Regards,<br /> Ray","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T12:55:24-07:00","id":1490163,"title":"","content":"Fire seems all but mandated. I'm also a big believer in general enhancements (nothing wrong with a sword that's extra good at cutting). Finally, perhaps a Flaw that puts your Scion at a disadvantage when interacting with Izanagi, Izanami, and their Scions might be appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","name":"yukikaze","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}